A command whose unreferenced functions each carry a record naming a code whose
subject is no declaration: a record of a document, a file or an import binding.
No such record matches a finding about a function, so each is stale, and none
marks its function live, so each function's own finding is reported beside it.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//deadset:ignore DS9003 -- a record
func record() {}

//deadset:ignore DS9004 -- a configured root
func root() {}

//deadset:ignore DS1601 -- a file
func built() {}

//deadset:ignore DS1602 -- a file
func imported() {}

//deadset:ignore DS1004 -- an import binding
func binding() {}
